   "widgets_values": [
    "Industrial rock, hammering machine percussion with metallic clangs, distorted bass, cold analog synth, shouted male lead with a gang chorus, gritty lo-fi production, relentless and mechanical",
    "[Verse]\nSteel is breathing in the dark\nPistons counting out the hour\nEvery window blind with sparks\nEvery hand a kind of power\nHammers fall like steady rain\nOn the anvil of the day\nWe are forging something nameless\nFrom the rust and from the clay\n\n[Chorus]\nIron heart, iron heart\nTurn the wheel and hold the line\nIron heart, iron heart\nEverything we build is mine\n\n[Verse]\nFurnace glow along the floor\nShadows walk the factory wall\nWe have heard the engines roar\nAnd we never once will fall\nOil and smoke and borrowed light\nEvery rivet set in time\nWe will work into the night\nTill the morning bells will chime\n\n[Chorus]\nIron heart, iron heart\nTurn the wheel and hold the line\nIron heart, iron heart\nEverything we build is mine\n\n[Bridge]\nAnd when the metal sings\nAnd when the silence breaks\nWe will know the shape of things\nBy everything it makes\n\n[Final Chorus]\nIron heart, iron heart\nTurn the wheel and hold the line\nIron heart, iron heart\nEverything we build is mine\n\n[Outro]\nTurn the wheel, turn the wheel\nHold the line",
    0.9900000000000002
