   "widgets_values": [
    "## ACE-Step v1 3.5B - the older song recipe (dev copy)\n\n**Why it exists:** the quality question is open (E13), and ACE-Step's *first* generation is a third MIT\ncandidate with a different recipe - `ace_step_v1_3.5b.safetensors` (7.3 GB, all-in-one, MIT) at **50 steps /\ncfg 5**, with `ModelSamplingSD3` (shift 5) and a **`LatentOperationTonemapReinhard`** operation applied\nthrough `LatentApplyOperationCFG` - none of which the 1.5 line uses. It is also the model the official\n**m2m editing** template edits with.\n\n**Built flat from `audio_ace_step_1_t2a_song.json`**, reading the text encoder's widget list verbatim from the\ntemplate (so `lyrics_strength` - a knob the 1.5 line dropped - is upstream's value); only `tags` and `lyrics`\nare replaced with the shared comparison input, seed 31, 120 s latent. **Unlike 1.5, v1's text encoder takes no\nduration**, so the length lives only on `EmptyAceStepLatentAudio.seconds` (single consumer).\n\n**What the m2m template showed (the restyle cost-out):** that route is `VAEEncodeAudio` -> `KSampler` at\n**denoise 0.3** - a *denoise-based edit*, i.e. the same mechanism E5 measured as **retention, not restyle**,\nso that limitation looks structural rather than a settings accident.\n\n**File:** `models/checkpoints/ace_step_v1_3.5b.safetensors` (MIT, `Comfy-Org/ACE-Step_ComfyUI_repackaged`,\n`all_in_one/`).\n\n*How to run it: story **S25** in `HOWTO.md`  ·  Why it is this way: **E13c** in `audio/EXPERIMENTS.md`.*\n"
   ],
